    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0634" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg622"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/4048</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3148</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-14">June 14, 1940</date>.<lb/>[Received June
                        20.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram No. 275 of
                    June 13, 8 p.m., I have the honor to transmit herewith a copy and translation of
                    the text of the official statement issued through the Department of Press and
                    Propaganda, for the purpose of clarifying the address which President <pb
                        facs="0635" n="623" xml:id="pg623"/> Vargas made on June 11, the text of
                    which was transmitted under cover of my despatch No. 3140 of even date.<anchor
                        n="55" xml:id="d736-f1"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Ambassador:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Randolph
                            Harrison, Jr.</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Second Secretary
                        of Embassy</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d736-a1.xml" xpointer="d736-a1"/>
            </div>
